   .article-content :global(.sidenote-checkbox:checked ~ .sidenote-text) {
     max-height: 16rem;
     opacity: 1;
     margin: 0.5rem 0;
     padding: 0.15rem 0 0.15rem 0.75rem;
   }
   /*
   * Wide screens: the note gets its own clearly bounded box —
   * bordered and lightly tinted, not just a loose float — and
   * the toggle is fully inert here, not merely styled to look
   * that way. Toggling only ever applies on narrower screens.
   *
   * Both selectors below (the plain one and the :checked one)
   * carry identical rules on purpose: the :checked variant has
   * higher specificity than a plain wide-screen override would,
   * so without repeating it here, clicking the number while on
   * a wide screen would still flip the margin back to the
   * mobile "expanded" values — visually reading as the note
   * jumping toward the text. Keeping both selectors in lockstep
   * guarantees checked state has zero visual effect at this
   * width.
   *
   * The numbers here are exact, not guessed: .article-layout
   * (above) reserves a real 12rem column with a 2rem gutter at
   * this same breakpoint, so width:12rem + margin-right:-14rem
   * (gutter + width) lands the note exactly in that column
